## Configuration profile
1. Open this page in Safari and tap the profile link above. Allow the download of the configuration profile.
2. Open Settings. Profile Downloaded appears at the top (or General, VPN & Device Management). Choose the profile, tap Install and enter your passcode.
3. iOS shows the profile as Not Signed. That is expected: it holds only the public root certificate and cannot be signed with a certificate your device does not trust yet. Compare the SHA-256 of the certificate with your trusted value before you install.
4. Open Settings, General, About, Certificate Trust Settings and switch on full trust for the root. Without this step the root is installed but not trusted for web sites.
Note: Menu names differ between iOS versions.
